      "content": "Custom Hash Functions"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "All the techniques and functions mentioned above are commonly used hash functions, but you're not limited to them."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Every problem is unique and might require a different hash function tailored to its characteristics."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Let's revisit the problem we started with:"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "Key-Value Mapping by Alphabetic Position of First Letter",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "In this case, the hash function used is:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "H(x) = ASCII(x[0]) - 64"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Clearly, this custom hash function doesn't fit into any of the techniques discussed earlier."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "This example underscores the fact that you must always select the appropriate hash function based on the specific requirements of your problem."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Your hash function might need to take into account the nature of the data, the expected distribution, and any patterns unique to your use case."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "So, feel free to design and experiment with your own hash functions to achieve the best results for your particular situation."
    },
